1
00:00:02,817 --> 00:00:08,427
Chart it before the next patient sits down. — Clock on screen. Nothing cut out.

2
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:19,388
One record. The note, the script and the order are tabs of it.

3
00:00:19,388 --> 00:00:27,466
Findings go in once.

4
00:00:27,466 --> 00:00:35,013
Same record. No new system.

5
00:00:35,013 --> 00:00:44,634
Medications are searched, not typed.

6
00:00:44,634 --> 00:00:48,831
Sent, and it lands on the chart.

7
00:00:48,831 --> 00:00:56,847
And the lab order, from the same place.

8
00:00:56,847 --> 00:01:03,901
Ordered by code, so the lab and the claim describe the same test.

9
00:01:03,901 --> 00:01:12,466
And who gets the result when it lands.

10
00:01:12,466 --> 00:01:17,281
The result files itself back to this chart. Nobody scans anything.

11
00:01:17,339 --> 00:01:23,059
One record. One pass. — Note, prescription and order — without leaving the chart.
